1
00:00:26,245 --> 00:00:29,655
(A place brimming with the spirit of youth)

2
00:00:29,785 --> 00:00:31,685
I haven't been in Sinchon for a long time.

3
00:00:31,685 --> 00:00:32,825
Same here. It's been a while.

4
00:00:32,825 --> 00:00:35,525
Didn't you come here often when you were in college?

5
00:00:35,525 --> 00:00:37,125
Oh, this place was great.

6
00:00:37,125 --> 00:00:39,095
- I loved it when I was in college.
- Right.

7
00:00:39,095 --> 00:00:40,865
- Sinchon.
- That's right.

8
00:00:40,865 --> 00:00:43,535
I didn't go to a university around Sinchon, though.

9
00:00:44,565 --> 00:00:45,705
(He just came here often.)

10
00:00:45,705 --> 00:00:47,305
- I know.
- This neighborhood...

11
00:00:47,405 --> 00:00:48,405
- Sogang University.
- My character in a drama...

12
00:00:48,405 --> 00:00:49,775
went to Yonsei University.

13
00:00:49,775 --> 00:00:50,805
- Really?
- Chil Bong.

14
00:00:50,805 --> 00:00:51,805
(Chil Bong went to Yonsei University.)

15
00:00:51,805 --> 00:00:53,045
- He went to Yonsei University?
- Yes.

16
00:00:53,045 --> 00:00:54,305
- Chil Bong went to Yonsei.
- I see.

17
00:00:54,475 --> 00:00:55,975
The university has a good baseball team.

18
00:00:55,975 --> 00:00:57,245
- Right.
- Yes.

19
00:00:57,245 --> 00:00:59,515
Yeon Shik already knows one of the Whenever Friends.

20
00:00:59,515 --> 00:01:00,745
Yes. I met...

21
00:01:00,745 --> 00:01:03,285
one of them at events.

22
00:01:03,285 --> 00:01:05,185
I've been a huge fan for a long time.

23
00:01:05,185 --> 00:01:07,555
I told him I wanted us to be good friends.

24
00:01:07,555 --> 00:01:09,055
I said hello to him.

25
00:01:09,155 --> 00:01:12,765
Well, that guy makes a lot of mistakes.

26
00:01:12,765 --> 00:01:13,965
- Really?
- Yes.

27
00:01:14,495 --> 00:01:16,395
From the image I have of him,

28
00:01:16,395 --> 00:01:18,235
he takes such good care of himself.

29
00:01:18,235 --> 00:01:21,065
- He's very disciplined.
- Yes. That's the image I have.

30
00:01:21,265 --> 00:01:23,735
He takes good care of him. But I'm not sure how he is now.

31
00:01:23,735 --> 00:01:25,605
He said he had hyperlipidemia.

32
00:01:26,075 --> 00:01:27,375
I'll ask him when he gets here.

33
00:01:27,875 --> 00:01:30,475
The weather is great today. It's not raining.

34
00:01:30,475 --> 00:01:31,745
I couldn't help it.

35
00:01:32,115 --> 00:01:34,485
(There was no news of rain today.)

36
00:01:34,915 --> 00:01:36,815
My gosh, I remember this street.

37
00:01:36,815 --> 00:01:38,555
- You do?
- Yes, I do.

38
00:01:39,655 --> 00:01:40,885
My gosh. That's my school.

39
00:01:40,885 --> 00:01:42,325
(Whenever Friend 1)

40
00:01:42,325 --> 00:01:45,395
Hey, when we were growing up, there were...

41
00:01:45,965 --> 00:01:48,095
- like 50 or 60 kids in 1 class.
- Like 50 to 60 kids.

42
00:01:48,965 --> 00:01:51,565
My gosh. There were so many kids out on the streets back then.

43
00:01:53,635 --> 00:01:55,065
Time flies.

44
00:01:55,575 --> 00:01:57,105
We're in our mid-40s now.

45
00:01:57,935 --> 00:02:00,445
(Tall, striking silhouettes that defy time)

46
00:02:00,445 --> 00:02:01,505
Let's go.

47
00:02:02,115 --> 00:02:03,215
I bet.

48
00:02:03,215 --> 00:02:05,115
(Walking up)

49
00:02:05,485 --> 00:02:07,485
- I can hear their footsteps.
- They're coming.

50
00:02:08,715 --> 00:02:09,885
I can hear the rain falling.

51
00:02:10,185 --> 00:02:11,385
- Oh, hey.
- Hello.

52
00:02:11,755 --> 00:02:13,025
- Gosh. Look at you.
- Hello.

53
00:02:13,025 --> 00:02:14,755
- You're wearing a cropped jacket.
- Right.

54
00:02:14,755 --> 00:02:16,255
(Today's Whenever Friends: Rain and Kim Jae Uck)

55
00:02:16,255 --> 00:02:17,295
Hello.

56
00:02:19,625 --> 00:02:23,135
(The ultimate king of male solo K-pop artists)

57
00:02:23,665 --> 00:02:27,635
(The performance king that took the world by storm)

58
00:02:27,835 --> 00:02:30,305
("Rain Joins the Korean Wave in Asia with 'Full House'")

59
00:02:30,475 --> 00:02:32,605
(He conquered Asia with his drama.)

60
00:02:32,875 --> 00:02:35,845
(He became an action star who broke into Hollywood.)

61
00:02:36,415 --> 00:02:39,015
(He still holds strong influence as a singer too.)

62
00:02:39,245 --> 00:02:41,485
(He's thriving across multiple fields.)

63
00:02:41,745 --> 00:02:44,385
(World Star Jung Ji Hoon, also known as Rain)

64
00:02:44,955 --> 00:02:46,355
(The irresistible handsome guy, Waffle Maker Seon Gi...)

65
00:02:46,355 --> 00:02:47,755
(in "Coffee Prince")

66
00:02:48,025 --> 00:02:51,255
(He was the original cold, aloof heartthrob with a chic allure.)

67
00:02:53,295 --> 00:02:57,035
(He transformed into a psychopath with a chilling gaze.)

68
00:02:59,465 --> 00:03:01,905
(With his lethally charming vibes,)

69
00:03:01,905 --> 00:03:04,475
(he conquered the romance scene too.)

70
00:03:05,345 --> 00:03:08,475
(The textbook definition of an unrivaled dark allure)

71
00:03:08,745 --> 00:03:11,745
(Actor Kim Jae Uck)

72
00:03:11,775 --> 00:03:13,485
- Hey, Ji Hoon.
- Hello.

73
00:03:13,485 --> 00:03:14,515
(Stylish guys are here.)

74
00:03:14,515 --> 00:03:15,655
- Hello.
- Have you been well?

75
00:03:15,655 --> 00:03:16,815
- Have you been well?
- Hey.

76
00:03:17,215 --> 00:03:19,555
- Jae Uck. Why...
- Yes, I'm here too.

77
00:03:20,085 --> 00:03:21,125
- It's been so long.
- Hello.

78
00:03:21,125 --> 00:03:22,395
- Hello.
- Hello.

79
00:03:22,395 --> 00:03:23,695
You're both wearing a leather jacket.

80
00:03:23,695 --> 00:03:25,295
Why are you wearing a leather jacket?

81
00:03:25,295 --> 00:03:27,095
It's not that. They told us to follow a dress code.

82
00:03:27,125 --> 00:03:28,425
- You...
- Our dress code was black denim.

83
00:03:28,425 --> 00:03:29,495
I heard it was black denim.

84
00:03:29,595 --> 00:03:30,595
Black denim.

85
00:03:30,595 --> 00:03:31,795
- I see.
- Your jeans.

86
00:03:32,105 --> 00:03:33,105
(What about Jae Uck?)

87
00:03:33,365 --> 00:03:34,405
Black and denim.

88
00:03:35,475 --> 00:03:36,535
That's how I understood it. Seriously.

89
00:03:36,535 --> 00:03:38,235
- I'm not joking.
- Black and denim?

90
00:03:38,235 --> 00:03:39,905
- It's not black and denim.
- So...

91
00:03:39,905 --> 00:03:41,915
My top is black, and my pants are denim.

92
00:03:41,915 --> 00:03:43,815
- I see. Jeans...
- Black denim...

93
00:03:43,815 --> 00:03:44,875
Are you wearing black denim?

94
00:03:44,875 --> 00:03:47,215
- Of course, I am.
- They're black jeans.

95
00:03:47,215 --> 00:03:48,885
- Black denim.
- I see.

96
00:03:48,885 --> 00:03:50,385
- Black jeans.
- Are you for real?

97
00:03:50,385 --> 00:03:51,715
- Are you the fashion police?
- What?

98
00:03:52,725 --> 00:03:54,425
- You guys...
- Look at you.

99
00:03:54,425 --> 00:03:56,255
- I can see your belly button.
- The leather jacket...

100
00:03:56,255 --> 00:03:58,525
- No.
- Why is your jacket so short?

101
00:03:58,525 --> 00:03:59,765
- It's not that.
- Okay.

102
00:03:59,995 --> 00:04:02,695
Jae Uck and I go to the same gym.

103
00:04:02,695 --> 00:04:04,635
- Really?
- We've been long-time members.

104
00:04:04,635 --> 00:04:06,135
We've been going there for a long time.

105
00:04:06,135 --> 00:04:07,605
When he comes to the gym,

106
00:04:07,805 --> 00:04:09,705
he focuses on stretching.

107
00:04:09,705 --> 00:04:11,035
- I see. So...
- Yes.

108
00:04:11,035 --> 00:04:12,545
you don't lift weights?

109
00:04:12,545 --> 00:04:14,375
I do lift weights.

110
00:04:14,375 --> 00:04:15,445
He mostly focuses on stretching.

111
00:04:15,445 --> 00:04:17,875
I hurt myself several times lifting weights without stretching.

112
00:04:17,875 --> 00:04:19,915
- Right.
- So I stretch a lot more now.

113
00:04:19,915 --> 00:04:21,955
Jae Uck stretches a lot.

114
00:04:22,115 --> 00:04:23,985
He doesn't talk much when he works out.

115
00:04:23,985 --> 00:04:26,085
No, he's chatty.

116
00:04:26,085 --> 00:04:28,025
He talks a lot when you encourage him.

117
00:04:28,025 --> 00:04:29,725
He talks a lot around people he's comfortable with.

118
00:04:29,725 --> 00:04:31,395
You were quiet because you felt uncomfortable.

119
00:04:31,395 --> 00:04:33,595
Well, I've known you for a very long time.

120
00:04:33,595 --> 00:04:34,895
- That's right.
- We met a long time ago.

121
00:04:34,895 --> 00:04:36,095
It's been 4 to 5 years.

122
00:04:36,095 --> 00:04:37,535
No, we met about 6 or 7 years ago.

123
00:04:37,535 --> 00:04:39,135
- Really?
- We met a long time ago.

124
00:04:40,735 --> 00:04:41,935
He's very precise.

125
00:04:42,075 --> 00:04:44,575
Whenever I saw Jae Seok,

126
00:04:44,575 --> 00:04:47,005
- I wanted to make small talk.
- Go on.

127
00:04:47,005 --> 00:04:50,415
But I don't know what I should talk about with you.

128
00:04:50,415 --> 00:04:51,575
I see. The topics.

129
00:04:51,575 --> 00:04:53,585
When I go to the gym, I always say hello to you...

130
00:04:53,585 --> 00:04:54,685
- politely.
- "Hello."

131
00:04:54,685 --> 00:04:56,385
- "Hello, sir."
- Then he'd stretch.

132
00:04:56,385 --> 00:04:57,615
We'd both work out.

133
00:04:57,615 --> 00:04:58,885
I'd say, "I'm leaving, sir."

134
00:04:58,885 --> 00:05:00,385
That was our interaction for 7 to 8 years.

135
00:05:00,385 --> 00:05:02,295
- Then...
- Wait. You go to the gym?

136
00:05:02,295 --> 00:05:03,525
- Of course.
- I see.

137
00:05:03,625 --> 00:05:05,695
You still lift weights, don't you?

138
00:05:06,225 --> 00:05:08,495
- I work out almost every day.
- Gosh.

139
00:05:08,495 --> 00:05:11,165
Actually, we talked about you before you came.

140
00:05:11,165 --> 00:05:14,505
You were quite worried about your cholesterol level back then.

141
00:05:14,505 --> 00:05:15,735
I have a fatty liver.

142
00:05:17,475 --> 00:05:20,445
Seriously. I work out a lot. How do I have a fatty liver?

143
00:05:20,445 --> 00:05:22,015
I told you, didn't I?

144
00:05:22,015 --> 00:05:23,745
- He loves food.
- Yes.

145
00:05:23,875 --> 00:05:25,645
When I saw you box in "Bloodhounds 2,"

146
00:05:25,645 --> 00:05:29,685
I was impressed with your boxing skills.

147
00:05:29,685 --> 00:05:30,855
He's been boxing for a long time.

148
00:05:30,855 --> 00:05:33,185
(While showing that his body never aged,)

149
00:05:33,185 --> 00:05:36,155
(he transformed into a powerful villain in "Bloodhounds 2.")

150
00:05:37,095 --> 00:05:38,895
Actually, I didn't train for a long time.

151
00:05:38,895 --> 00:05:41,725
I did six-month intensive training for this drama.

152
00:05:41,725 --> 00:05:42,865
That's when I learned.

153
00:05:42,865 --> 00:05:45,535
That I shouldn't even try to spar...

154
00:05:45,535 --> 00:05:47,965
with those boxers. I shouldn't even try anything.

155
00:05:47,965 --> 00:05:50,405
It's just their reflexes.

156
00:05:50,405 --> 00:05:52,075
They can easily dodge anything.

157
00:05:52,075 --> 00:05:54,105
- Compared to regular people... Yes.
- Their reflexes are crazy, right?

158
00:05:54,105 --> 00:05:56,945
- We look at people with our pupils.
- That's true.

159
00:05:56,945 --> 00:05:58,985
But they can see everything with the whites of their eyes.

160
00:05:58,985 --> 00:06:00,985
Their peripheral vision is crazy.

161
00:06:00,985 --> 00:06:02,855
- So even a slight movement...
- Not with the whites of their eyes.

162
00:06:02,855 --> 00:06:04,755
Right. They can't see with the whites of their eyes.

163
00:06:05,385 --> 00:06:06,555
That's not possible.

164
00:06:06,855 --> 00:06:08,525
I just meant it figuratively.

165
00:06:08,685 --> 00:06:09,755
They can't see with the whites of their eyes.

166
00:06:09,755 --> 00:06:11,395
- You meant it figuratively.
- Right. It's just my feeling.

167
00:06:11,395 --> 00:06:13,765
- They have a wide range of vision.
- That's right.

168
00:06:13,765 --> 00:06:15,595
- It's just my feeling. Yes.
- That's it, right?

169
00:06:15,595 --> 00:06:16,695
Okay.

170
00:06:16,895 --> 00:06:18,065
What were we talking about?

171
00:06:18,735 --> 00:06:20,665
- Boxing.
- We were talking about boxing.

172
00:06:20,665 --> 00:06:22,535
Ji Hoon is fun to tease.

173
00:06:23,205 --> 00:06:24,675
Ji Hoon is one of my favorites.

174
00:06:24,835 --> 00:06:26,975
- Gosh.
- He's fun to tease on TV shows.

175
00:06:27,275 --> 00:06:29,015
- Right away.
- I got this vibe from you...

176
00:06:29,015 --> 00:06:30,745
when I was walking in earlier.

177
00:06:30,745 --> 00:06:33,545
You didn't seem happy to see me.

178
00:06:34,285 --> 00:06:35,345
- Oh, hey.
- Hello.

179
00:06:35,345 --> 00:06:38,555
(A sour expression)

180
00:06:39,085 --> 00:06:41,225
- You usually welcome your guests.
- But...

181
00:06:41,225 --> 00:06:42,525
- You didn't look happy today.
- Listen.

182
00:06:42,525 --> 00:06:44,455
As I told you earlier, when he walked in,

183
00:06:44,455 --> 00:06:47,865
his cropped leather jacket caught my eye.

184
00:06:47,925 --> 00:06:49,795
- I thought it was too much.
- Right.

185
00:06:49,795 --> 00:06:51,895
- Actually...
- Hold on.

186
00:06:51,895 --> 00:06:54,205
- What?
- What if someone else wore this?

187
00:06:54,205 --> 00:06:55,605
- Yes?
- Would you have been this honest?

188
00:06:55,605 --> 00:06:57,535
- I can't do that to other people.
- Right?

189
00:06:57,535 --> 00:06:59,145
I'm only saying it because it's you, Ji Hoon.

190
00:06:59,475 --> 00:07:00,605
(Chuckling)

191
00:07:00,605 --> 00:07:03,375
I would've said this to Jae Uck too if we were close.

192
00:07:03,975 --> 00:07:05,515
That he looked like a detective from the Japanese colonial era.

193
00:07:07,415 --> 00:07:09,255
- The jacket looks good on him.
- Right, it does.

194
00:07:09,255 --> 00:07:11,785
- He just needs a mustache here.
- Right. He looks like...

195
00:07:11,785 --> 00:07:12,785
(A villainous detective)

196
00:07:12,785 --> 00:07:14,055
- He'd be perfect for that role.
- Yes.

197
00:07:14,485 --> 00:07:16,755
Right. You know those mean detectives?

198
00:07:17,095 --> 00:07:19,895
So are you guys close or something?

199
00:07:19,895 --> 00:07:22,665
Actually, we're both in a brunch club.

200
00:07:22,665 --> 00:07:24,435
(A brunch club)

201
00:07:24,835 --> 00:07:25,965
(Smirking)

202
00:07:25,965 --> 00:07:27,605
- That doesn't suit you guys.
- Wait. Jae Seok.

203
00:07:27,605 --> 00:07:28,765
- What is it?
- Hold on.

204
00:07:28,765 --> 00:07:30,735
- Wait. Why did you smirk like that?
- What?

205
00:07:30,735 --> 00:07:32,805
Why is he in so many clubs?

206
00:07:32,805 --> 00:07:34,775
- Right. Both of them...
- I'm not in that many clubs.

207
00:07:34,775 --> 00:07:36,115
You're in a lot of clubs.

208
00:07:36,115 --> 00:07:38,375
- Like what?
- You're in a motorcycle club.

209
00:07:38,375 --> 00:07:39,485
- Right?
- It's just us two.

210
00:07:39,485 --> 00:07:40,885
- It's the same club?
- Yes, the motorcycle club.

211
00:07:40,885 --> 00:07:41,945
I see.

212
00:07:41,945 --> 00:07:43,715
- It's just us.
- I see.

213
00:07:43,715 --> 00:07:44,755
Don't you ride a motorcycle as well?

214
00:07:44,755 --> 00:07:46,285
- I do. But...
- Right.

215
00:07:46,285 --> 00:07:48,655
I only checked the engine a couple of times this year.

216
00:07:48,925 --> 00:07:50,495
I barely went out for a ride.

217
00:07:50,495 --> 00:07:51,655
You've been busy.

218
00:07:51,655 --> 00:07:53,565
He starts a lot of hobbies.

219
00:07:53,565 --> 00:07:54,765
But he never follows through.

220
00:07:55,895 --> 00:07:58,465
- I can't hold onto them.
- Camping,

221
00:07:58,465 --> 00:07:59,905
- coffee making, - Right.

222
00:07:59,905 --> 00:08:01,535
- and so on.
- Yes.

223
00:08:01,535 --> 00:08:02,805
He's interested in a lot of things.

224
00:08:02,805 --> 00:08:04,335
I like to dabble in them.

225
00:08:05,375 --> 00:08:07,845
(Yeon Seok is an expert at dabbling.)

226
00:08:08,145 --> 00:08:10,045
So you guys are in a motorcycle club.

227
00:08:10,045 --> 00:08:11,475
- Yes.
- Right.

228
00:08:11,475 --> 00:08:13,115
Let me explain our relationship.

229
00:08:13,115 --> 00:08:16,655
We like to meet spontaneously without any pressure or obligations.

230
00:08:16,655 --> 00:08:19,185
So we hang out and talk about our lives.

231
00:08:19,185 --> 00:08:21,725
Like what we've been doing and so on.

232
00:08:21,725 --> 00:08:24,295
Our conversations are light and simple.

233
00:08:24,295 --> 00:08:26,465
(Best friends who freely share stories about their lives)

234
00:08:27,025 --> 00:08:29,165
We meet only a couple of times throughout the year.

235
00:08:29,165 --> 00:08:30,435
- We call and text.
- Right.

236
00:08:30,435 --> 00:08:31,695
- Things are always the same.
- Right.

237
00:08:31,695 --> 00:08:34,335
This year is almost over. How many times did you meet up?

238
00:08:34,335 --> 00:08:36,105
- Once. Or twice?
- Did we meet up twice?

239
00:08:36,105 --> 00:08:37,675
- We went to Sokcho together.
- Right.

240
00:08:37,675 --> 00:08:38,945
- We met up twice.
- We met up twice.

241
00:08:39,045 --> 00:08:41,245
- So you keep it pressure-free.
- Yes.

242
00:08:41,245 --> 00:08:42,775
- That's a great relationship.
- Right.

243
00:08:42,775 --> 00:08:44,575
I have a question.

244
00:08:44,575 --> 00:08:47,685
Yeon Seok. Have you ever had a meal with Jae Seok...

245
00:08:47,685 --> 00:08:48,715
outside work?

246
00:08:48,715 --> 00:08:50,985
Not during a shoot. Just in a private setting.

247
00:08:50,985 --> 00:08:53,185
We had coffee together just once.

248
00:08:53,385 --> 00:08:55,285
- And he bought me a barbecue meal.
- Then...

249
00:08:55,285 --> 00:08:56,525
- Really?
- Yes.

