00:17:25,335 --> 00:17:27,965
(They only work out for 45 minutes.)

499
00:17:28,205 --> 00:17:31,905
(A group exercise without a break)

500
00:17:33,905 --> 00:17:35,975
(Weightlifting, cardio, and bodyweight exercises...)

501
00:17:35,975 --> 00:17:38,075
(all in one cycle)

502
00:17:38,215 --> 00:17:41,785
(The gym is full of motivated members.)

503
00:17:42,645 --> 00:17:45,055
(She's in charge of training her clients.)

504
00:17:45,385 --> 00:17:48,255
(The manager and owner of the gym)

505
00:17:48,255 --> 00:17:50,325
How's business? Do you have a lot of clients?

506
00:17:50,525 --> 00:17:52,095
I do.

507
00:17:52,255 --> 00:17:54,695
- But it's a college town.
- Right.

508
00:17:54,695 --> 00:17:57,165
During midterms, finals, or semester breaks,

509
00:17:57,165 --> 00:18:00,535
- they often come and go.
- They have to study for midterms.

510
00:18:00,535 --> 00:18:01,705
- Right.
- I see.

511
00:18:01,805 --> 00:18:04,635
Having a lot of clients is one thing.

512
00:18:04,635 --> 00:18:07,445
But when they sign up to 30 classes, they need to come regularly.

513
00:18:07,445 --> 00:18:09,205
- Right. Yes.
- Right?

514
00:18:09,205 --> 00:18:10,475
- That's why...
- Okay.

515
00:18:10,475 --> 00:18:11,915
I don't recommend session packages.

516
00:18:11,915 --> 00:18:13,385
- Really?
- When they buy session packages,

517
00:18:13,385 --> 00:18:14,485
they don't come.

518
00:18:14,485 --> 00:18:15,615
- They don't.
- Right.

519
00:18:15,615 --> 00:18:16,785
- People who go on...
- Go on.

520
00:18:16,785 --> 00:18:17,955
business trips a lot...

521
00:18:17,955 --> 00:18:19,655
buy session packages.

522
00:18:19,925 --> 00:18:22,485
I tell them to come every day and make it...

523
00:18:22,485 --> 00:18:23,895
- Right.
- into a routine.

524
00:18:23,895 --> 00:18:25,325
- Right.
- Come early if they have plans.

525
00:18:25,855 --> 00:18:27,295
Come in the evening if they don't have plans.

526
00:18:27,295 --> 00:18:28,725
- I knew it.
- Come twice if they're free.

527
00:18:28,725 --> 00:18:30,565
She sounds very firm as I expected.

528
00:18:30,565 --> 00:18:33,465
She's been managing her clients for years.

529
00:18:33,765 --> 00:18:35,335
I also work out at a gym.

530
00:18:35,335 --> 00:18:37,435
I've been busy, so I couldn't go to the gym lately.

531
00:18:37,575 --> 00:18:39,845
- The coach must be disappointed.
- Right.

532
00:18:39,845 --> 00:18:42,375
I bought the 30-session package, but I haven't gone in a while.

533
00:18:42,375 --> 00:18:44,175
That's why session packages are no good.

534
00:18:44,715 --> 00:18:45,775
That's not good.

535
00:18:45,775 --> 00:18:47,485
- She's firm.
- As the gym's manager...

536
00:18:47,485 --> 00:18:50,055
- It's hard to manage the gym then.
- Of course.

537
00:18:50,215 --> 00:18:52,885
We read your introduction letter earlier.

538
00:18:52,885 --> 00:18:55,125
- It said you had a different job.
- Yes.

539
00:18:55,125 --> 00:18:57,655
You decided to run this gym because you got into fitness?

540
00:18:57,655 --> 00:19:00,725
I had my previous job for ten years.

541
00:19:00,725 --> 00:19:02,725
I worked at a hospital.

542
00:19:02,865 --> 00:19:06,235
I wanted to quit after working there for ten years.

543
00:19:06,235 --> 00:19:08,765
- Right.
- So I quit my job with no regrets.

544
00:19:08,965 --> 00:19:10,575
Then I moved to Seoul.

545
00:19:10,735 --> 00:19:12,505
I met my husband, and we got married.

546
00:19:12,505 --> 00:19:13,775
Then I settled down here.

547
00:19:13,775 --> 00:19:16,445
Do you and your husband work out together?

548
00:19:16,545 --> 00:19:19,145
Before our child was born,

549
00:19:19,215 --> 00:19:21,845
working out together at 7am was our routine.

550
00:19:21,845 --> 00:19:23,915
- We always worked out at 7am.
- That's great.

551
00:19:23,915 --> 00:19:25,555
- Together?
- Yes, we worked out together.

552
00:19:25,555 --> 00:19:26,725
Then we started our own day.

553
00:19:27,225 --> 00:19:28,955
(Workout dates from their dating days...)

554
00:19:28,955 --> 00:19:30,755
(all the way to her full-term pregnancy)

555
00:19:30,855 --> 00:19:31,925
(Exercising with her husband)

556
00:19:31,925 --> 00:19:37,335
(She went to the gym every morning before giving birth.)

557
00:19:37,565 --> 00:19:39,635
We used to work out together all the time.

558
00:19:39,635 --> 00:19:42,205
But my husband has been busy lately. So he hasn't been working out.

559
00:19:42,465 --> 00:19:44,475
He turned into a piggie. But...

560
00:19:44,805 --> 00:19:45,975
A piggie?

561
00:19:46,245 --> 00:19:47,645
- Wait. A piggie?
- A piggie.

562
00:19:47,805 --> 00:19:49,345
- A piggie.
- I see.

563
00:19:49,345 --> 00:19:50,815
Where did you grow up then?

564
00:19:50,815 --> 00:19:53,245
- I'm from Gwangju.
- I see.

565
00:19:53,415 --> 00:19:55,415
- You're from Gwangju.
- Yes.

566
00:19:55,615 --> 00:19:56,915
That's why I wrote to your show.

567
00:19:56,915 --> 00:19:59,955
I really wanted to meet celebrities.

568
00:20:00,685 --> 00:20:03,625
- I live in Yeouido now.
- Okay.

569
00:20:03,755 --> 00:20:05,155
I never ran into a celebrity.

570
00:20:05,155 --> 00:20:06,865
You could see a lot of celebrities...

571
00:20:06,865 --> 00:20:08,565
- in Yeouido back in the day.
- Right.

572
00:20:08,565 --> 00:20:10,635
You're the first celebrities I met.

573
00:20:11,035 --> 00:20:12,335
- It's us four?
- Today?

574
00:20:12,335 --> 00:20:13,405
(Meeting celebrities for the first time)

575
00:20:13,405 --> 00:20:15,905
- So I'm very nervous now.
- I see.

576
00:20:15,905 --> 00:20:18,335
And Ji Hoon and Jae Uck are joining us today.

577
00:20:18,335 --> 00:20:20,305
I was so shocked. It's like watching TV.

578
00:20:20,305 --> 00:20:21,605
You guys look exactly the same.

579
00:20:21,605 --> 00:20:23,675
(Starstruck)

580
00:20:23,675 --> 00:20:26,345
How's your life in Seoul?

581
00:20:26,345 --> 00:20:27,445
Do you like living here?

582
00:20:27,445 --> 00:20:28,885
Actually, I'm a homebody.

583
00:20:28,885 --> 00:20:30,285
So I rarely leave Yeouido.

584
00:20:30,285 --> 00:20:32,455
I only go back and forth between Yeouido and Sinchon.

585
00:20:32,455 --> 00:20:34,785
- Yeouido has everything too.
- Yes.

586
00:20:34,785 --> 00:20:37,025
That's right. They renovated the 63 Building.

587
00:20:37,025 --> 00:20:39,455
- Have you been there?
- They renovated the observatory.

588
00:20:39,455 --> 00:20:40,895
The first floor looks amazing too.

589
00:20:40,895 --> 00:20:42,795
- The first floor too?
- All the famous cafes are there.

590
00:20:42,795 --> 00:20:44,495
- They all open there.
- There's a gallery too.

591
00:20:44,495 --> 00:20:45,995
- There was an aquarium too.
- Yes.

592
00:20:45,995 --> 00:20:47,265
- It's gone now.
- It's no longer there.

593
00:20:47,265 --> 00:20:48,665
- They moved to Jeju.
- It's... I see.

594
00:20:48,665 --> 00:20:50,735
- Really?
- They moved to Jeju Island.

595
00:20:50,735 --> 00:20:52,605
- Yeouido is great.
- Yes, it's great.

596
00:20:52,605 --> 00:20:54,105
That's why there are so many cafes now.

597
00:20:54,105 --> 00:20:55,545
I was there two days ago.

598
00:20:55,545 --> 00:20:57,315
- It sounds like you're at a cafe.
- Are they...

599
00:20:57,945 --> 00:20:59,175
So...

600
00:20:59,175 --> 00:21:01,285
I can't even see Jae Uck that well.

601
00:21:01,845 --> 00:21:04,215
- Do you want me to get lost?
- No.

602
00:21:05,485 --> 00:21:06,685
- No.
- Jae Uck...

603
00:21:06,685 --> 00:21:08,755
- Yes?
- is a calm one.

604
00:21:08,755 --> 00:21:10,795
- I know. I've seen him on TV.
- You do, right?

605
00:21:10,795 --> 00:21:12,855
- How do you know that?
- I saw him on TV.

606
00:21:13,765 --> 00:21:15,565
How does she know that? Wait.

607
00:21:15,565 --> 00:21:17,035
- This is...
- Ji Hoon.

608
00:21:17,035 --> 00:21:19,495
- I...
- She can just feel the vibe.

609
00:21:19,635 --> 00:21:20,905
I can't let this slide.

610
00:21:21,265 --> 00:21:22,535
How do you know that?

611
00:21:22,535 --> 00:21:24,075
- I told you I was a homebody.
- You're a homebody.

612
00:21:24,075 --> 00:21:25,275
- You watch a lot of TV?
- Yes, totally.

613
00:21:25,275 --> 00:21:27,445
- Do you watch a lot of dramas?
- And variety shows.

614
00:21:27,445 --> 00:21:29,645
I watch a lot of dramas too.

615
00:21:29,645 --> 00:21:32,115
When did you get married?

616
00:21:32,215 --> 00:21:35,815
I got married three years ago.

617
00:21:35,815 --> 00:21:37,485
How's it going?

618
00:21:37,485 --> 00:21:39,155
- You and your husband...
- Yes.

619
00:21:39,155 --> 00:21:41,625
were dating... Why do you suddenly look so down?

620
00:21:41,825 --> 00:21:44,595
When we were dating, we never fought.

621
00:21:45,195 --> 00:21:46,765
- We never fought.
- Go on.

622
00:21:46,995 --> 00:21:48,865
But marriage is like a war.

623
00:21:49,195 --> 00:21:51,165
- We just...
- What do you argue about?

624
00:21:51,465 --> 00:21:55,565
It's like... "Why did you leave the tofu in the fridge like this?"

625
00:21:55,565 --> 00:21:58,175
"Why didn't you put the tofu..."

626
00:21:58,605 --> 00:22:00,705
- "in a separate food container?"
- Right.

627
00:22:00,705 --> 00:22:02,175
- Or he should've covered it up.
- Right.

628
00:22:02,175 --> 00:22:03,645
He said he was going to eat it later.

629
00:22:03,645 --> 00:22:04,845
- When he said that...
- He was going to eat it soon.

630
00:22:04,845 --> 00:22:06,175
Right. He said he was going to eat it soon.

631
00:22:06,175 --> 00:22:07,985
Then he said, "Have you ever cleaned the fridge?"

632
00:22:07,985 --> 00:22:09,445
"Why are you nagging me when you never clean the fridge?"

633
00:22:09,445 --> 00:22:10,885
- The subject changed then.
- Right.

634
00:22:10,885 --> 00:22:12,485
- It went into cleaning habits.
- And...

635
00:22:12,585 --> 00:22:14,485
"Wait, a year ago..."

636
00:22:15,055 --> 00:22:16,825
Who brought that up? Your husband?

637
00:22:16,925 --> 00:22:19,355
- Well, it was probably me.
- Don't do that.

638
00:22:19,555 --> 00:22:21,325
- It was me.
- Don't bring up the past.

639
00:22:21,325 --> 00:22:23,435
- A year ago...
- Are you speaking on his behalf?

640
00:22:23,435 --> 00:22:25,165
Listen. It's not cool.

641
00:22:25,165 --> 00:22:27,065
Bringing up what happened a year ago...

642
00:22:27,065 --> 00:22:30,235
When they started talking, he upset her.

643
00:22:30,235 --> 00:22:31,705
- We argue over nothing.
- Exactly.

644
00:22:31,975 --> 00:22:34,345
Once he started mentioning small things, I did the same.

645
00:22:34,545 --> 00:22:36,845
- You guys do that?
- She's just pointing things out.

646
00:22:36,845 --> 00:22:38,445
- Do you do that too, Jae Seok?
- Do what?

647
00:22:38,445 --> 00:22:40,715
- Do this to your wife?
- If something like this happens,

648
00:22:41,415 --> 00:22:44,055
I apologize right away. "Okay. I forgot to do that."

649
00:22:44,815 --> 00:22:46,285
"I'll do that next time."

650
00:22:46,285 --> 00:22:47,825
That's one thing.

651
00:22:47,955 --> 00:22:50,225
But my husband has a lot of social gatherings.

652
00:22:50,655 --> 00:22:51,825
What gatherings?

653
00:22:51,925 --> 00:22:54,065
- He must be a busy guy.
- He goes out to have drinks...

654
00:22:54,065 --> 00:22:55,365
- Are you on board with that?
- with his friends.

655
00:22:55,965 --> 00:22:57,295
We fought a lot about that too.

656
00:22:57,835 --> 00:23:00,635
Let's say you go to a work get-together twice a week.

657
00:23:01,005 --> 00:23:02,805
Then is it okay to meet your friends spontaneously twice a week?

658
00:23:02,805 --> 00:23:04,905
- Gosh. No.
- No way. He has no conscience.

659
00:23:05,175 --> 00:23:06,445
- Because of that... Yes.
- Two impromptu get-togethers?

660
00:23:06,445 --> 00:23:08,475
You reached a conclusion without listening to our answers.

661
00:23:08,945 --> 00:23:11,115
Gosh. I'm at a disadvantage here.

662
00:23:11,115 --> 00:23:12,175
You could side with my husband.

663
00:23:12,175 --> 00:23:15,615
- You know what? I sympathized...
- You're all guys.

664
00:23:15,615 --> 00:23:17,155
- with what she said.
- Right.

665
00:23:17,155 --> 00:23:19,385
He already goes to a work get-together twice a week.

666
00:23:19,385 --> 00:23:21,085
- Right.
- Two impromptu get-togethers?

667
00:23:21,085 --> 00:23:22,425
That's too much.

668
00:23:22,425 --> 00:23:23,725
- That's too much.
- That's...

669
00:23:23,725 --> 00:23:25,625
- It's too much, right?
- I can't allow that.

670
00:23:25,625 --> 00:23:28,025
What line of work is your husband in?

671
00:23:28,025 --> 00:23:29,495
Why does he have a work get-together twice a week?

672
00:23:29,495 --> 00:23:31,465
- That's a lot of get-togethers.
- Right.

673
00:23:31,465 --> 00:23:32,495
- I was wondering that too.
- People don't have...

674
00:23:32,495 --> 00:23:33,535
- that many get-togethers now.
- There aren't...

675
00:23:33,535 --> 00:23:34,865
- that many work get-togethers now.
- Right.

676
00:23:34,865 --> 00:23:36,775
- Right.
- Should I check then?

677
00:23:36,775 --> 00:23:38,875
Wait. We didn't...

678
00:23:39,105 --> 00:23:40,945
That's not why we asked you.

679
00:23:41,445 --> 00:23:45,415
Depending on the line of work, some people might have to meet up...

680
00:23:45,815 --> 00:23:48,745
- with a lot of people.
- Right.

681
00:23:48,985 --> 00:23:52,115
He used to work at an asset management firm.

682
00:23:52,415 --> 00:23:54,625
Then he quit his job.

683
00:23:54,625 --> 00:23:57,725
Now, he works at a start-up company.

684
00:23:57,725 --> 00:23:59,255
That's understandable...

685
00:23:59,255 --> 00:24:00,795
- if he works at a start-up.
- Right.

686
00:24:00,795 --> 00:24:02,495
- They must meet with clients.
- The thing is...

687
00:24:02,495 --> 00:24:05,035
- He might have business meetings.
- He must have many meetings.

688
00:24:05,035 --> 00:24:08,965
- The company is growing now.
- Right.

689
00:24:08,965 --> 00:24:10,535
- You should be understanding.
- That's understandable.

690
00:24:10,535 --> 00:24:12,435
He works at an asset management firm. His hands are tied.

691
00:24:12,435 --> 00:24:13,945
That's the job he quit.

692
00:24:14,805 --> 00:24:17,145
(Ambushing him with her fact-checking move)

693
00:24:17,145 --> 00:24:19,275
- Earlier...
- I know he works at a start-up.

694
00:24:19,275 --> 00:24:21,645
- He quit that job.
- That was his former job.

695
00:24:21,645 --> 00:24:23,115
- That was his old job.
- He used to work there.

696
00:24:23,115 --> 00:24:24,385
I can't give out wrong information.

697
00:24:24,385 --> 00:24:26,285
- He doesn't work at the firm.
- He doesn't.

698
00:24:26,285 --> 00:24:28,585
She has a hard time letting things go too.

699
00:24:28,585 --> 00:24:30,125
- Even the slightest mistake...
- No.

700
00:24:30,125 --> 00:24:31,955
- I'm easygoing. Yes.
- You are?

701
00:24:31,955 --> 00:24:35,095
We're not here to give them marital advice.

702
00:24:35,325 --> 00:24:36,735
(Having an identity crisis rather late)

703
00:24:36,735 --> 00:24:39,765
Anyway, since we're here today,

704
00:24:39,905 --> 00:24:43,235
- we should hype up her day.
- Yes.

705
00:24:43,235 --> 00:24:45,005
- Could you start with this?
- Okay.

706
00:24:45,475 --> 00:24:46,575
Okay.

707
00:24:47,545 --> 00:24:48,705
Read it, please.

708
00:24:48,845 --> 00:24:50,145
I'm really nervous.

709
00:24:50,445 --> 00:24:52,775
"The mom, the dad, and even their ten-month-old son..."

710
00:24:52,775 --> 00:24:54,515
"are serious about fitness."

711
00:24:54,515 --> 00:24:56,345
"Three pairs of Nike family sneakers."

712
00:24:56,345 --> 00:24:58,155
(Round 1 present: 3 pairs of Nike family sneakers)

713
00:24:58,155 --> 00:25:00,585
I've been wearing these sneakers for over three years.

714
00:25:00,685 --> 00:25:02,525
- Really?
- Yes, it's been over three years.

715
00:25:02,525 --> 00:25:05,425
My son can't walk yet. So this is his first pair.

716
00:25:05,655 --> 00:25:06,695
- That's great.
- Yes.

717
00:25:06,765 --> 00:25:08,825
- Can I see the baby sneakers?
- Yes, go ahead.

718
00:25:08,825 --> 00:25:10,295
- Go on.
- I bet they're cute.

719
00:25:11,435 --> 00:25:12,965
Oh, so cute.

720
00:25:13,365 --> 00:25:14,565
It's so cute.

721
00:25:14,865 --> 00:25:17,605
- We've been there. You know?
- Of course.

722
00:25:17,605 --> 00:25:19,175
Thank you for giving me his first sneakers.

723
00:25:19,175 --> 00:25:21,205
- Right. They're not mine yet.
- Exactly.

724
00:25:21,205 --> 00:25:22,975
- We'll try to win them for you.
- Okay.

725
00:25:23,105 --> 00:25:24,575
(Spare 45)

726
00:25:24,575 --> 00:25:25,975
(They have 45 seconds...)

727
00:25:25,975 --> 00:25:28,215
(to complete 4 exercises.)

728
00:25:28,245 --> 00:25:29,715
- Spare 45?
- Spare 45.

729
00:25:30,215 --> 00:25:32,955
(Spare 45)

730
00:25:33,255 --> 00:25:37,095
(A 4-stage spare time mission)

731
00:25:40,825 --> 00:25:41,825
(40kg sled)

732
00:25:41,825 --> 00:25:43,195
- Oh, that thing you push.
- That one.

733
00:25:43,195 --> 00:25:44,795
- This one?
- This one?

734
00:25:45,635 --> 00:25:46,735
Do we have to cross the line?

735
00:25:46,735 --> 00:25:47,735
(Finish line)

736
00:25:47,935 --> 00:25:50,175
- Just reach the line.
- Just reach the line?

737
00:25:51,105 --> 00:25:52,935
- Jae Seok, this is...
- Good?

738
00:25:52,935 --> 00:25:55,145
- I'll do it.
- Okay. What's next?

739
00:25:55,145 --> 00:25:57,745
The second player has to...

740
00:25:57,845 --> 00:25:59,275
(Ball, cone)

741
00:25:59,275 --> 00:26:01,885
(Jump onto the box and back down...)

